##########################################################################
# AceOutpost-ApplicationRelease - BuildMaster OtterScript Plan
#
# !! EDITING THIS FILE IS NOT ENOUGH - SYNC IT TO THE RAFT !!
#   BuildMaster executes the copy of this plan stored in its raft, NOT this
#   file. Committing a change here does nothing until you run:
#       Sync-BuildMasterPlans -Path <thisFile> -IncludePipelines
#   The paired stage runner (Invoke-ApplicationReleaseStage.ps1) IS read from disk
#   at run time, so a commit that changes both leaves the raft passing the OLD
#   argument list to the NEW parameter block. When the missing argument is a
#   [Parameter(Mandatory)] one, PowerShell prompts a console that nobody can
#   answer and the stage HANGS FOREVER with no error. See
#       SolutionDocumentation/BuildMaster-Plan-Raft-Sync-Requirement.md
##########################################################################
# Task 16.79. AceOutpost thin adapter, mirroring AceCommander-ApplicationRelease.otter.
# The bundle is built, signed and uploaded to releasebundle-experimental by
# ApplicationBuild-1Stage; this plan only verifies and promotes those immutable bytes
# Experimental -> Development -> Integration -> QA -> Production. No rebuilding above
# Experimental, database apply, service install, or Distribution stage.
#
# Variables (Release/Application Variables - set in BuildMaster, never secrets):
#   $ApplicationReleaseRunner           - <ATAP.Utilities worktree>\src\ATAP.Utilities.BuildTooling.BuildMaster\Plans\Invoke-ApplicationReleaseStage.ps1
#   $ApplicationReleaseContext          - release-context.json written by the ApplicationBuild-1Stage build
#   $ApplicationReleaseContextSha256    - Operator-approved SHA-256 of that context
#   $ApplicationReleaseWorkingDirectory - Committed ATAP.Utilities worktree
set $ReleaseBuildId = $BuildMasterId(build);
InedoCore::Exec
(
    FileName: pwsh,
    Arguments: >>-NonInteractive -File "$ApplicationReleaseRunner" -ContextPath "$ApplicationReleaseContext" -ExpectedContextSha256 "$ApplicationReleaseContextSha256" -Stage "$PipelineStageName" -BuildId "$ReleaseBuildId">>,
    WorkingDirectory: $ApplicationReleaseWorkingDirectory,
    SuccessExitCode: 0
);
